meta {
  name: Delete Branch
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/branches/{{branchId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  branchId: 095ce801-16db-438a-9f26-4fa65d15c88c
}

docs {
  🔒 **RBAC:** requires `business_admin:center_and_operations__delete_branch` — enforced by `PermissionGuard` (`@RequirePermission`). A caller whose effective permissions (user override ?? branch-role override ?? role baseline) lack this get **403 `PERMISSION_DENIED`**; the `business_admin` / `administrator` roles bypass all checks, so `{{businessAccessToken}}` (an admin) still succeeds here.
  
  Soft-delete a branch (sets `deletedAt` and `status: INACTIVE`). Scoped to the
  caller's tenant. In the same transaction, everything that grants access through
  the branch is detached:
  - every staff assignment at the branch is revoked (`isActive=false`,
    `deletedAt`/`revokedAt` set, `revokedBy` = caller) — it disappears from the
    profile switcher and the Edit User form;
  - user-level permission overrides and branch-role permission overrides at the
    branch are deleted;
  - the branch's module enablement is disabled (drops out of every
    "branches with module X" list and business-admin "all branches" scope).
  Historical data (orders, patients, settings, audit) is not touched. Users
  logged in at the branch land on their default profile at their next token
  refresh (≤ 15 min). The main branch cannot be deleted (409
  CANNOT_DELETE_MAIN_BRANCH).
}
